{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"autositic-relaxative-nurseshark","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\nThe src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler cohort contains audited comments or docstrings that obscure current behavior with repetition, obvious narration, duplicated explanation, or historical detail. The audit is pinned to `9e65567b79ffe872534c3c656ade7b34340d8192`.\n\n## Approach\nEdit explanatory text only in this directory/subsystem cohort. Condense it to current, non-obvious rationale and constraints; retain every file-specific preserve item and consumer contract below. Grouping adjacent files from one subsystem keeps the change reviewable in one session and permits one coherent verification pass without changing executable behavior.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py:142-158, 242-247, 327-333, 480-498, 534-539, 570-587` — Preserve registration-before-exec, auth classification, context-manager lifetime, and lock-steal/migration behavior. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_backend.py:1-30, 103-121, 161-195, 218-242, 336-354, 609-624, 670-690` — Preserve backend roles, capability narrowing, uncached conformance, and the `RemoteRef.instance` limitation. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_field_contract.py:1-35` — Preserve the per-field symmetry and removal-policy contract. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_loader.py:1-30` — Preserve canonical module keys and registration-before-execution. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_ref_lock_push.py:1-56, 66-72, 119-121` — Preserve remote CAS atomicity, force-with-lease behavior, and fail-closed outcomes. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/access_check.py:267-279` — Preserve the mapped-project visibility preflight and non-raising result boundary. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/_base.py:1-12, 41-60, 81-89, 116-151` — Preserve logging at swallowed-error boundaries and the advancing offset pager. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/_hierarchy.py:1-9, 51-74, 110-194` — Preserve v2 pagination, sub-task versus Epic Link writes, and fresh read-back verification. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/_issues.py:40-47, 53-60, 80-87, 103-151, 166-187, 201-217, 242-254, 283-300` — Preserve create payload translation, object-valued fields, transition routing, and additive labels. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/_people.py:1-17, 46-73, 111-131, 162-174` — Preserve DC username identity, unassignment classification, and verbatim property values. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py:1-16, 50-106, 131-135, 183-190, 217-234, 269-341, 396-432, 460-493, 540-545` — Preserve shared mapping, DC codec/comment limits, explicit identity resolver, and captured deployment scope. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/retry.py:1-16, 29-56, 151-164, 192-218` — Preserve translated error shapes, retry-after handling, bounded backoff, and single retry choke point. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/settings.py:1-26, 51-105` — Preserve precedence, required token handling, defaults, and immutable captured settings. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/transitions.py:1-16, 34-79, 133-149` — Preserve name/destination matching and ambiguity refusal. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/